name: sim.readProximitySensor
description: Reads the state of a proximity sensor. This function doesn't perform detection, it merely reads the result from a previous call to sim.handleProximitySensor
luaSynopsis: int res, float dist, list point, int obj, list n = sim.readProximitySensor(int sensorHandle)
pythonSynopsis: int res, float dist, float[3] point, int obj, float[3] n = sim.readProximitySensor(int sensorHandle)
inputs:
1. sensorHandle: handle of a proximity sensor
outputs:
1. res: detection state (0 or 1)
2. dist: distance to the detected point
3. point: array of 3 numbers indicating the relative coordinates of the detected point
4. obj: handle of the object that was detected
5. n: normal vector (normalized) of the detected surface. Relative to the sensor reference frame
replacedBy:
- name: detectedNormal, class: proximitySensor, file: proximitySensor_detectedNormal.property
- name: detectedObject, class: proximitySensor, file: proximitySensor_detectedObject.property
- name: detectedPoint, class: proximitySensor, file: proximitySensor_detectedPoint.property
